    "prompt": "TWO-PIECE SET — PROFESSIONAL HANGER ARRANGEMENT\n\nIf REFERENCE IMAGE 2 contains a matching two-piece outfit, first identify the exact construction of BOTH garments before placing them on the hanger.\n\nThe final arrangement must look like a REAL clothing store or fashion creator physically prepared the complete outfit on ONE hanger for presentation.\n\nCRITICAL STRUCTURAL RULE:\n\nUse ONLY the original hanger from REFERENCE IMAGE 1.\n\nThere must be ONE hanger total.\n\nNEVER generate:\n- a second hanger\n- an additional horizontal rod\n- a transparent support bar\n- a floating clip rail\n- a second hook\n- invisible suspension hardware\n\nIf clips are required, attach them DIRECTLY to the existing horizontal wooden bar of the original hanger.\n\nExactly TWO small garment clips maximum.\n\nThe clips must look physically attached to the original hanger itself.\n\n\nSTEP 1 — IDENTIFY THE UPPER GARMENT:\n\nDetermine how the upper garment would physically hang in real life.\n\nIf the upper garment has shoulders or sleeves:\nplace it normally over the two sloped shoulders of the hanger.\n\nThe hanger sits naturally INSIDE the garment.\n\nIf the upper garment has thin straps:\nplace each strap naturally over the corresponding side of the hanger.\n\nIf the upper garment is strapless, bandeau, tube top, cropped strapless top, or another garment with NO shoulders and NO straps:\n\nDO NOT fold it over the wooden bar.\n\nDO NOT wrap it around the hanger.\n\nDO NOT drape it loosely over the bar.\n\nInstead, suspend the strapless upper garment in a physically believable retail-display position using appropriate discreet attachment to the existing hanger structure.\n\nKeep the entire front of the top facing the camera.\n\nThe neckline/top edge remains naturally horizontal.\n\nThe garment hangs vertically.\n\nPreserve its real width, shape and proportions.\n\nIt must look intentionally displayed, not improvised.\n\n\nSTEP 2 — IDENTIFY THE LOWER GARMENT:\n\nIf the set contains shorts, pants or a skirt, preserve that piece as a completely separate physical garment.\n\nPosition the lower garment directly underneath the upper garment.\n\nKeep the FRONT of the lower garment facing the camera.\n\nKeep the waistband naturally horizontal.\n\nSuspend the waistband using EXACTLY TWO small realistic garment clips.\n\nLEFT CLIP:\nattached near the left side of the waistband.\n\nRIGHT CLIP:\nattached near the right side of the waistband.\n\nBoth clips must connect physically to the ORIGINAL hanger structure.\n\nNO SECOND BAR.\n\nNO TRANSPARENT BAR.\n\nNO FLOATING SUPPORT.\n\nNO INVISIBLE HANGER.\n\n\nPROFESSIONAL SET PRESENTATION:\n\nThe two garments should form ONE visually cohesive vertical outfit:\n\nUPPER GARMENT\n↓\nsmall natural visual spacing\n↓\nLOWER GARMENT\n\nDo NOT overlap the garments excessively.\n\nDo NOT create a huge empty gap between them.\n\nUse only a small realistic separation so the viewer can immediately understand the complete set.\n\nThe upper and lower pieces must be independently readable.\n\nBoth pieces face forward.\n\nBoth pieces remain centered relative to the hanger.\n\nThe outfit should feel balanced without becoming artificially symmetrical.\n\n\nIMPORTANT — DO NOT FOLD THE PRODUCT FOR CONVENIENCE:\n\nNever solve the hanging problem by folding, rolling or wrapping a garment around the hanger.\n\nDo not fold a strapless top over the horizontal bar.\n\nDo not roll the waistband.\n\nDo not bend the garment into an unnatural shape.\n\nThe purpose is PRODUCT PRESENTATION.\n\nThe visible front design of each garment should remain clean and recognizable.\n\n\nCLIPS:\n\nClips must be SMALL, discreet and realistic.\n\nUse simple neutral retail garment clips.\n\nThey should not become a visual focal point.\n\nThe clips must physically grip the fabric.\n\nCreate subtle realistic compression exactly where each clip contacts the garment.\n\nNo floating clips.\n\nNo giant clips.\n\nNo decorative clips.\n\nNo duplicated clips.\n\nNo clip rail.\n\nNo extra horizontal structure.\n\n\nNATURAL GRAVITY:\n\nEvery garment hangs downward because of gravity.\n\nThe attachment points support the weight.\n\nFabric immediately below each attachment point develops subtle natural vertical tension.\n\nAllow slight natural asymmetry.\n\nAllow very small gravity folds.\n\nDo NOT make either garment perfectly flat like a catalog cutout.\n\nDo NOT make the garments float.\n\nDo NOT make them rigid.\n\nDo NOT stretch them unnaturally to fit the hanger.\n\n\nPRODUCT FIDELITY:\n\nThe hanging method may change the SPATIAL POSITION of the fabric, but NEVER the PRODUCT DESIGN.\n\nPreserve both pieces exactly from REFERENCE IMAGE 2:\n\nsame color\nsame material\nsame texture\nsame ribbing\nsame prints\nsame graphics\nsame neckline\nsame waistband\nsame drawstrings\nsame pockets\nsame seams\nsame stitching\nsame sleeves\nsame leg openings\nsame cut\nsame length\nsame width\nsame proportions\n\nIf the shorts have a drawstring, preserve the exact drawstring.\n\nIf the fabric is ribbed, preserve the exact ribbed appearance.\n\nIf the top is cropped, keep it cropped.\n\nNever redesign either piece.\n\n\nVISUAL HIERARCHY:\n\nThe hanger should support the outfit, not compete with it.\n\nThe upper garment occupies the upper presentation area.\n\nThe lower garment hangs naturally below.\n\nKeep enough separation to clearly show:\nthe complete upper garment,\nits bottom hem,\nthe complete waistband of the lower garment,\nand the overall silhouette of the lower garment.\n\nThe final composition must look deliberately prepared for a TikTok Shop clothing demonstration.\n\n\nFINAL PHYSICAL REALISM CHECK:\n\nBefore generating the final image, verify:\n\nCan every garment's weight be visually traced to a real attachment point?\n\nYES.\n\nIs there only ONE original hanger?\n\nYES.\n\nAre there any floating bars or invented hanger structures?\n\nNO.\n\nIs any garment unnaturally folded around the hanger?\n\nNO.\n\nAre both pieces clearly recognizable as the exact products from IMAGE 2?\n\nYES.\n\nDoes the arrangement look physically possible in the real world?\n\nYES.\n\nThe final result must look like a REAL PERSON manually arranged the complete matching set on ONE REAL HANGER before taking the photograph.\n\nNOT A COLLAGE.\nNOT A DIGITAL OVERLAY.\nNOT A FLOATING OUTFIT.\nNOT TWO HANGERS.\nNOT A TRANSPARENT CLIP BAR.\nNOT A GARMENT WRAPPED AROUND THE HANGER.\n\nONE REAL HANGER.\nTWO REAL GARMENTS.\nPHYSICALLY CORRECT ATTACHMENT.\nNATURAL GRAVITY.\nPROFESSIONAL PRODUCT PRESENTATION.\nULTRA-REALISTIC SMARTPHONE PHOTOGRAPHY.",
