    "prompt": "Create an ultra-realistic clothing replacement using TWO reference images.\n\nREFERENCE IMAGE 1 = MASTER INFLUENCER AND SCENE.\nREFERENCE IMAGE 2 = EXACT PANTS / JEANS PRODUCT SOURCE.\n\nGOAL:\n\nReplace ONLY the pants currently worn by the person in REFERENCE IMAGE 1 with the EXACT pants shown in REFERENCE IMAGE 2.\n\nThe final result must look like the influencer was genuinely wearing the pants from IMAGE 2 when IMAGE 1 was originally photographed.\n\nThis is a CLOTHING REPLACEMENT, not a redesign and not a new image generation.\n\nREFERENCE PRIORITY:\n\nIMAGE 1 controls:\n- exact person\n- identity\n- face\n- hair\n- skin\n- body proportions\n- body position\n- pose\n- torso\n- arms\n- hands\n- legs\n- feet\n- smartphone or accessories\n- environment\n- background\n- furniture\n- lighting\n- shadows\n- camera angle\n- perspective\n- framing\n- composition\n\nIMAGE 2 controls ONLY the replacement pants.\n\nDo NOT transfer the model, body, background, pose, lighting or environment from IMAGE 2.\n\nPANTS REPLACEMENT:\n\nCompletely remove the visual appearance of the original pants from IMAGE 1 and replace them with the EXACT pants from IMAGE 2.\n\nPreserve the product identity from IMAGE 2 with maximum fidelity.\n\nPreserve exactly:\n- original color\n- wash\n- material\n- fabric texture\n- cut\n- silhouette\n- rise\n- waistband design\n- belt loops\n- front closure\n- buttons\n- zipper area\n- pockets\n- pocket placement\n- seams\n- stitching\n- panels\n- graphics\n- logos\n- labels\n- distressing\n- fading\n- leg width\n- taper\n- cuffs\n- hem\n- length\n- design details\n\nDo NOT create a similar pair of pants.\n\nUse the SAME PRODUCT represented in IMAGE 2.\n\nBODY FIT — CRITICAL:\n\nRealistically fit the replacement pants onto the EXISTING body from IMAGE 1.\n\nDO NOT reshape the person's body to fit the pants.\n\nThe PANTS must adapt naturally to the existing anatomy, pose and perspective.\n\nPreserve the exact:\n- waist position\n- hip position\n- thigh anatomy\n- knee position\n- leg orientation\n- leg length\n- stance\n- foot placement\n\nThe replacement pants must follow the real three-dimensional shape of the person's legs.\n\nIf one leg is bent, the pants must bend naturally at that knee.\n\nIf one leg is closer to the camera, preserve correct perspective.\n\nIf the legs are separated, maintain the correct independent shape of each pant leg.\n\nDo NOT change the pose.\n\nDo NOT straighten or reposition the legs.\n\nDo NOT enlarge or reduce the person's thighs.\n\nDo NOT change body proportions.\n\nFIT AND SIZE:\n\nInfer the intended fit from IMAGE 2.\n\nIf the product is loose, preserve a naturally loose fit.\n\nIf it is straight-cut, preserve a straight silhouette.\n\nIf it is slim, preserve that structure.\n\nIf it is wide-leg, preserve the correct width.\n\nDo NOT automatically make the pants tight to the body.\n\nDo NOT make loose pants skinny.\n\nDo NOT make fitted pants oversized.\n\nPreserve the product's original design while realistically adapting its scale to the influencer.\n\nREALISTIC FABRIC PHYSICS:\n\nReconstruct ONLY the temporary fabric folds required by the person's existing pose.\n\nCreate physically believable tension and compression around:\n- waist\n- hips\n- crotch\n- upper thighs\n- knees\n- lower legs\n- ankles\n\nFolds must result naturally from gravity, body position and fabric structure.\n\nDo NOT copy impossible folds from IMAGE 2 if IMAGE 2 uses a different pose.\n\nPreserve the MATERIAL and DESIGN from IMAGE 2 while calculating realistic folds for the pose in IMAGE 1.\n\nNo rubber-like fabric.\nNo melted fabric.\nNo artificial wrinkles.\nNo floating fabric.\nNo warped seams.\n\nWAISTBAND AND SHIRT OCCLUSION — EXTREMELY IMPORTANT:\n\nRespect the existing relationship between the upper garment and pants in IMAGE 1.\n\nIf the shirt covers part of the waistband, KEEP THAT SAME AREA COVERED.\n\nDo NOT lift the shirt to reveal the replacement pants.\n\nDo NOT shorten the shirt.\n\nDo NOT tuck or untuck the shirt.\n\nDo NOT move the shirt.\n\nDo NOT expose hidden skin.\n\nDo NOT expose additional waistband merely to display product details.\n\nAny portion of the replacement pants hidden by the shirt must remain naturally hidden.\n\nThe replacement pants must appear physically UNDERNEATH the shirt where appropriate.\n\nUPPER CLOTHING ABSOLUTE LOCK:\n\nEverything worn above the pants remains EXACTLY as shown in IMAGE 1.\n\nDo NOT change:\n- shirt\n- T-shirt\n- jacket\n- hoodie\n- accessories\n- sleeves\n- neckline\n- garment position\n- garment color\n- garment folds\n\nDo NOT allow the replacement operation to modify the upper garment.\n\nFOOTWEAR LOCK:\n\nPreserve the exact footwear or socks from IMAGE 1.\n\nThe replacement pants must naturally meet, overlap or end above the existing footwear according to their real length.\n\nDo NOT replace footwear.\n\nOCCLUSION:\n\nRespect all real foreground/background relationships.\n\nHands that overlap the pants remain naturally in front.\n\nThe shirt remains naturally in front where applicable.\n\nObjects in the scene remain correctly positioned.\n\nDo NOT allow the pants to pass through hands, legs, shirt, footwear or surrounding objects.\n\nLIGHTING:\n\nIMAGE 2 provides PRODUCT IDENTITY.\n\nIMAGE 1 provides FINAL LIGHTING.\n\nRelight the replacement pants naturally according to IMAGE 1.\n\nMatch:\n- light direction\n- brightness\n- exposure\n- white balance\n- shadow softness\n- ambient light\n- reflections\n- photographic contrast\n\nDo NOT preserve incompatible lighting from IMAGE 2.\n\nSCENE LOCK:\n\nDo not modify the background.\n\nDo not modify the room.\n\nDo not modify the mirror.\n\nDo not modify the person's face.\n\nDo not modify the person's body.\n\nDo not modify the camera.\n\nDo not modify the framing.\n\nDo not beautify or regenerate the influencer.\n\nReplace ONLY the pants.\n\nFINAL REALISM CHECK:\n\nThe result must NOT look like pants were pasted onto a person.\n\nThe pants must have:\n- real volume\n- correct anatomy\n- correct perspective\n- realistic fabric weight\n- realistic folds\n- correct occlusion\n- natural shadows\n- accurate product details\n\nThe final photograph must look like IMAGE 1 was originally captured with the influencer already wearing the EXACT pants from IMAGE 2.\n\nIMAGE 1 = PERSON + BODY + POSE + SCENE + LIGHTING.\nIMAGE 2 = PANTS ONLY.\n\nCHANGE ONLY THE PANTS.\n\nNO BODY TRANSFORMATION.\nNO POSE CHANGE.\nNO SHIRT CHANGE.\nNO PRODUCT REDESIGN.\nNO COLOR CHANGE.\nNO INVENTED DETAILS.\nNO EXTRA LIMBS.\nNO SCENE MODIFICATION.\nNO AI-LOOKING FABRIC.\n\nULTRA-REALISTIC.\nPHOTOREALISTIC.\nAUTHENTIC SMARTPHONE PHOTOGRAPHY.",
