    "description": "Prompt de troca de camiseta do influenciador Boomerang.",
    "prompt": "Create an ultra-realistic clothing replacement using TWO reference images.\n\nREFERENCE IMAGE 1 = MASTER INFLUENCER AND SCENE.\nREFERENCE IMAGE 2 = EXACT TOP / T-SHIRT PRODUCT SOURCE.\n\nGOAL:\n\nReplace ONLY the upper garment currently worn by the person in REFERENCE IMAGE 1 with the EXACT upper garment shown in REFERENCE IMAGE 2.\n\nThe final result must look like the influencer was genuinely wearing the garment from IMAGE 2 when IMAGE 1 was originally photographed.\n\nThis is a PRECISE CLOTHING REPLACEMENT.\n\nDo NOT regenerate the person.\nDo NOT recreate the scene.\nDo NOT redesign the product.\n\nREFERENCE PRIORITY:\n\nIMAGE 1 controls:\n- exact person\n- identity\n- face\n- hair\n- skin\n- neck\n- shoulders\n- chest anatomy\n- torso proportions\n- arms\n- hands\n- fingers\n- pose\n- lower clothing\n- pants\n- footwear\n- accessories\n- smartphone\n- environment\n- background\n- lighting\n- camera angle\n- perspective\n- framing\n- composition\n\nIMAGE 2 controls ONLY the replacement upper garment.\n\nDo NOT transfer the person, pose, body, background or environment from IMAGE 2.\n\nGARMENT REPLACEMENT:\n\nCompletely replace the visual appearance of the original upper garment in IMAGE 1 with the EXACT garment shown in IMAGE 2.\n\nPreserve the product identity with maximum visual fidelity.\n\nPreserve exactly:\n- original color\n- color distribution\n- fabric appearance\n- texture\n- material\n- wash\n- pattern\n- print\n- graphics\n- text\n- logos\n- labels\n- neckline\n- collar\n- shoulder construction\n- sleeves\n- sleeve length\n- cuffs\n- seams\n- stitching\n- panels\n- buttons\n- zippers\n- pockets\n- hem\n- cut\n- width\n- length\n- silhouette\n- proportions\n- every visible design detail\n\nDo NOT create a similar garment.\n\nUse the EXACT PRODUCT represented in IMAGE 2.\n\nBODY FIT — CRITICAL:\n\nFit the replacement garment naturally onto the EXISTING influencer.\n\nDO NOT change the influencer's body to accommodate the garment.\n\nPreserve the exact:\n- neck position\n- shoulder width\n- chest proportions\n- torso length\n- waist position\n- arm position\n- elbow position\n- wrist position\n- hand position\n- posture\n\nThe replacement garment must conform naturally to this existing anatomy.\n\nSHOULDERS:\n\nThe garment's shoulder seams must sit in physically believable positions according to its original cut.\n\nDo not make shoulders unnaturally narrow or wide.\n\nSLEEVES:\n\nSleeves must follow the exact existing arm position.\n\nIf an arm is bent, reconstruct natural sleeve folds around the shoulder and elbow.\n\nIf an arm is raised, the fabric must respond naturally.\n\nDo NOT move the arm to simplify the garment.\n\nDo NOT generate another arm.\n\nDo NOT alter the hand.\n\nNECKLINE:\n\nPlace the neckline naturally around the existing neck.\n\nPreserve the exact neckline design from IMAGE 2.\n\nDo NOT enlarge the neck opening.\n\nDo NOT distort the collar.\n\nDo NOT change the person's neck.\n\nDo NOT expose skin that should naturally remain covered.\n\nFIT AND SILHOUETTE:\n\nInfer the intended fit from IMAGE 2.\n\nIf oversized, preserve realistic oversized volume.\n\nIf regular-fit, preserve regular proportions.\n\nIf fitted, preserve the intended fitted silhouette.\n\nIf cropped, preserve the authentic crop length.\n\nIf long, preserve the appropriate length.\n\nDo NOT automatically tighten the garment against the body.\n\nDo NOT make oversized clothing fitted.\n\nDo NOT make fitted clothing oversized.\n\nPreserve the PRODUCT'S CUT while adapting it realistically to the influencer's existing body.\n\nREALISTIC FABRIC PHYSICS:\n\nReconstruct natural fabric behavior according to the influencer's pose.\n\nAllow physically believable folds around:\n- shoulders\n- chest\n- underarms\n- elbows\n- waist\n- side seams\n- lower hem\n\nFabric folds must respond to:\ngravity,\nbody volume,\narm position,\nmaterial weight,\nand garment construction.\n\nDo NOT copy incompatible folds from IMAGE 2.\n\nIMAGE 2 defines the garment.\n\nIMAGE 1 defines how that garment must physically behave in the final pose.\n\nNo floating fabric.\nNo melted fabric.\nNo plastic appearance.\nNo excessive wrinkles.\nNo impossible stretching.\nNo fabric morphing.\n\nLOWER GARMENT — ABSOLUTE LOCK:\n\nThe pants, jeans, shorts, skirt or any lower garment from IMAGE 1 must remain 100% UNCHANGED.\n\nPreserve exactly:\n- color\n- texture\n- waistband\n- pockets\n- seams\n- fit\n- folds\n- position\n- length\n- proportions\n\nDo NOT modify the pants while replacing the shirt.\n\nDo NOT recolor them.\n\nDo NOT redesign them.\n\nDo NOT move the waistband.\n\nDo NOT change the leg fit.\n\nHEM AND WAIST INTERACTION:\n\nDetermine naturally how the replacement upper garment overlaps the existing lower garment.\n\nThe replacement shirt must follow its REAL length and cut from IMAGE 2.\n\nIf the shirt naturally extends over the waistband, it must physically overlap the pants.\n\nIf the original product is cropped, preserve its authentic crop.\n\nDo NOT tuck the garment unless IMAGE 2 clearly defines that construction and the requested replacement requires it.\n\nDo NOT randomly tuck one side.\n\nDo NOT roll the hem.\n\nDo NOT artificially lift the shirt to expose the pants.\n\nCreate physically correct fabric layering.\n\nHANDS AND ARMS — ABSOLUTE ANATOMY LOCK:\n\nPreserve every visible arm, hand and finger from IMAGE 1.\n\nDo NOT generate additional arms.\n\nDo NOT generate additional hands.\n\nDo NOT remove an arm.\n\nDo NOT reposition hands.\n\nDo NOT change finger anatomy.\n\nDo NOT allow sleeves to consume or merge with hands.\n\nIf a hand or arm overlaps the shirt, preserve correct foreground occlusion.\n\nThe new garment exists physically BEHIND any arm or hand that is in front of the torso.\n\nACCESSORY LOCK:\n\nPreserve all existing accessories from IMAGE 1 unless they are physically underneath the garment.\n\nSmartphone remains unchanged.\n\nWatch remains unchanged.\n\nBracelets remain unchanged.\n\nNecklace remains unchanged when physically visible.\n\nDo NOT invent accessories from IMAGE 2.\n\nLIGHTING:\n\nIMAGE 2 provides PRODUCT IDENTITY.\n\nIMAGE 1 provides FINAL LIGHTING.\n\nRelight the replacement garment according to IMAGE 1.\n\nMatch:\n- light direction\n- exposure\n- white balance\n- ambient light\n- highlight softness\n- shadows\n- contrast\n- photographic texture\n\nThe shirt must naturally cast subtle shadows on the body and lower garment where physically appropriate.\n\nDo NOT retain incompatible studio lighting from IMAGE 2.\n\nSCENE LOCK:\n\nThe environment remains EXACTLY IMAGE 1.\n\nNo background changes.\nNo furniture changes.\nNo lighting changes.\nNo camera changes.\nNo crop changes.\nNo pose changes.\nNo face changes.\nNo body changes.\n\nReplace ONLY the upper garment.\n\nFINAL REALISM CHECK:\n\nThe garment must look physically WORN by the influencer.\n\nNot pasted onto the torso.\n\nNot digitally overlaid.\n\nNot floating.\n\nNot painted onto the body.\n\nThere must be believable:\n- volume\n- fabric thickness\n- gravity\n- folds\n- sleeve behavior\n- shoulder placement\n- neckline placement\n- occlusion\n- shadows\n- perspective\n\nThe final result must look like IMAGE 1 was originally photographed with the influencer genuinely wearing the EXACT upper garment from IMAGE 2.\n\nIMAGE 1 = PERSON + ANATOMY + POSE + LOWER CLOTHING + SCENE + LIGHTING.\nIMAGE 2 = UPPER GARMENT ONLY.\n\nCHANGE ONLY THE UPPER GARMENT.\n\nNO FACE CHANGE.\nNO BODY CHANGE.\nNO PANTS CHANGE.\nNO POSE CHANGE.\nNO EXTRA LIMBS.\nNO PRODUCT REDESIGN.\nNO COLOR CHANGE.\nNO INVENTED DETAILS.\nNO SCENE MODIFICATION.\n\nULTRA-REALISTIC.\nPHOTOREALISTIC.\nAUTHENTIC SMARTPHONE PHOTOGRAPHY.",
